A||||4||Raydar||Car Stereo Question - New Pioneer head units. ||||5||
Z||000000||Raydar||07-31-2000||09:57 PM||||Does anybody know if the new Pioneer "IP bus" head units (like Cliff and others have purchased) are capable of controlling other manufacturers CD changers. (Like Kenwood or Alpine?) <BR>I know this is a shot in the dark.  I am only asking because I have seen situations where several different brands (don't remember which ones) of changers actually were manufactured by the same company. Would really like to *not* have to spend another $200 for another changer.   <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula||08-01-2000||09:56 AM||||they should be universal...but Ive heard of stereo stuff not being compatible... I cant give you an answer that I know would be correct so Im going to say I dont know. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||b lo 0||08-01-2000||11:35 AM||||Nope, you can't.  Unfortunately, the connectors are different as are the coded messages going to the head unit (track, disc, time).  I've had several people try this before, and even if it does hook up, it won't work.  Sorry to be the bearer of bad news.  I have to get a new changer to hook up to my Kenwood head unit, even though I already have Blaupunkt and Sony units.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">    <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||08-01-2000||12:10 PM||||Formula and B lo...<BR>Thanks for your answers. I suspected that even if the connectors matched, the protocols would be different. Thought there <I>might</I> be an outside chance that they were compatible, though. That would be too easy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Thanks again<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||08-03-2000||04:34 PM||||You have to wonder if the protocols might be the same, but the pinout of the cables is purposely different....||||reg||1
